From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:11:48 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 353/353] DOS-PORT: patch 0353 -- release flavour: no
 rb_max_spr_* tracking (0351 review F2)

The largest-sprite-per-frame dimensions (patch 0166) are read only by the skipframe
attribution line, which ags 0351 compiles out of the DOSAGS_RELEASE flavour, and reset
only there too. In release they were still updated per composited sprite with no reader
and no reset. Gated the same way; the instrumented flavour is unchanged.
---
 Engine/gfx/ali3dsw.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Engine/gfx/ali3dsw.cpp b/Engine/gfx/ali3dsw.cpp
index 6c445404f..f9af123ae 100644
--- a/Engine/gfx/ali3dsw.cpp
+++ b/Engine/gfx/ali3dsw.cpp
@@ -794,12 +794,14 @@ size_t SDLRendererGraphicsDriver::RenderSpriteBatch(const ALSpriteBatch &batch,
         // every tail frame, an unchanged overlay is being recomposited --
         // the class that produced every win that landed today. If they
         // vary, it is real content and the answer is different.
+#ifndef DOSAGS_RELEASE   // patch 0353: only the skipframe line reads these, and 0351 compiles it out
         if (_w * _h > dos_port_tick_timing.rb_max_spr_px)
         {
             dos_port_tick_timing.rb_max_spr_px = _w * _h;
             dos_port_tick_timing.rb_max_spr_w = _w;
             dos_port_tick_timing.rb_max_spr_h = _h;
         }
+#endif
     }
 #endif
     int drawAtX = sprite.x + surf_offx;
